From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Bruno=20Greg=C3=B3rio?= <accounts@bruno.pw>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 15:00:08 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] WIP: arm64: dts: qcom: sm6450-sony-xperia-columbia-pdx246:
 Raise the regulator floors
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The regulator windows come from the stock tree, but few mainline
consumers set a voltage: not ufshcd, not the QMP and Femto PHYs, not the
DSI host. For an RPMh rail it cannot read back, the regulator core
applies the bottom of the window, so those rails came up below the
voltage the vendor driver starts them at, its qcom,init-voltage. UFS's
VCCQ sat at 1.08 V and VCCQ2 at 1.62 V, both under the UFS minimum.

Raise the fourteen floors that are below that voltage to it. The ceilings
are unchanged.

To be folded into the SM6450 DT / board DT once it has probed on the device.

Signed-off-by: Bruno Gregório <accounts@bruno.pw>
